tus codes, request validation, response formatting, and rate limiting. Apply when creating API routes, handling errors, validating input, or designing API responses."},"features":{"zh":["错误处理","状态码","请求验证","响应格式化","限速","API路由创建"],"ja":["エラーハンドリング","ステータスコード","リクエスト検証","レスポンス形式","レート制限","APIルートの作成"],"ko":["오류 처리","상태 코드","요청 검증","응답 형식","속도 제한","API 루트 생성"],"es":["Manejo de errores y excepciones","Validación de solicitudes y respuestas","Limitación de velocidad y escalabilidad","Diseño de APIs RESTful","Implementación de seguridad y autenticación"],"fr":["Gestion d''erreurs et d''exceptions","Validation des requêtes et des réponses","Limitation de débit et évolutivité","Conception d''API RESTful","Mise en œuvre de la sécurité et de l''authentification"],"de":["Fehlerbehandlung und Ausnahmen","Anfrage- und Antwortvalidierung","Rate Limiting und Skalierbarkeit","Entwurf von RESTful-APIs","Implementierung von Sicherheit und Authentifizierung"],"pt":["Tratamento de erros e exceções","Status codes e resposta personalizada","Validação de solicitações e parâmetros","Rate limiting e controle de acesso","Desenvolvimento de APIs REST com Node.js e Python"],"ru":["Обработка ошибок и исключений","Статус-коды и настраиваемые ответы","Валидация запросов и параметров","Контроль скорости запросов и доступа","Разработка REST API с использованием Node.js и Python"],"ar":["معالجة الأخطاء والاستثناءات","أكواد الحالة والاستجابة المخصصة","تصديق الطلبات والparameters","التحكم في معدل الطلبات والوصول","بناء واجهات برمجة التطبيقات باستخدام Node.js و Python"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用AI智能开发构建REST API","API开发工具","REST API开发框架","API错误处理","API状态码","API请求验证","API响应格式化","API限速","API开发教程"],"ja":["AIエージェントを使用してREST APIを開発する方法","API開発ツール","REST API開発フレームワーク","APIエラーハンドリング","APIステータスコード","APIリクエスト検証","APIレスポンス形式","APIレート制限","API開発ガイド"],"ko":["AI 에이전트를 사용하여 REST API를 개발하는 방법","API 개발 도구","REST API 개발 프레임워크","API 오류 처리","API 상태 코드","API 요청 검증","API 응답 형식","API 속도 제한","API 개발 가이드"],"es":["desarrollo de api","agentes de ia para desarrollo de api","cómo crear una api rest","validación de solicitudes en api","limitación de velocidad en api","seguridad en api","autenticación en api","alternativas a postman","desarrollo de api con node js"],"fr":["développement d''api","outils d''ia pour développement d''api","comment créer une api rest","validation des requêtes en api","limitation de débit en api","sécurité en api","authentification en api","alternatives à postman","développement d''api avec node js"],"de":["api-entwicklung","ki-tools für api-entwicklung","wie man eine rest-api erstellt","anfragevalidierung in api","rate limiting in api","sicherheit in api","authentifizierung in api","alternativen zu postman","api-entwicklung mit node js"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de api","ferramentas de ia","api rest","tratamento de erros","validação de solicitações","node js","python","desenvolvimento de software","ia para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["разработка api","ии агенты","rest api","обработка ошибок","валидация запросов","node js","python","разработка программного обеспечения","ии для разработчиков"],"ar":["تطوير واجهات برمجة التطبيقات","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","واجهات برمجة التطبيقات","معالجة الأخطاء","تصديق الطلبات","node js","python","تطوير البرمجيات","الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T04:13:19.579Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"API Development","description":"Build REST APIs with proper error handling, status codes, request validation, response formatting, and rate limiting. Apply when creating API routes, handling errors, validating input, or designing API responses.","version":"1.1.0","bodyPreview":"# API Development\n\nSystematic REST API development with error handling, validation, and consistent response formats.\n\n## Overview\n\nThis Skill enforces:\n- HTTP status codes (appropriate, not overused)\n- RFC 7807 Problem Details for errors\n- Input validation and sanitization\n- Consistent response formatting\n- Request correlation IDs\n- Rate limiting\n- Security-first error messages\n- Centralized error handling\n\nApply when building API routes, handling errors, or designing responses.\n\n## HTTP Status","body":"# API Development\n\nSystematic REST API development with error handling, validation, and consistent response formats.\n\n## Overview\n\nThis Skill enforces:\n- HTTP status codes (appropriate, not overused)\n- RFC 7807 Problem Details for errors\n- Input validation and sanitization\n- Consistent response formatting\n- Request correlation IDs\n- Rate limiting\n- Security-first error messages\n- Centralized error handling\n\nApply when building API routes, handling errors, or designing responses.\n\n## HTTP Status Codes\n\n### Status Code Categories\n\n| Range | Purpose | Common Examples |\n|-------|---------|-----------------|\n| 200-299 | Success | 200 OK, 201 Created, 204 No Content |\n| 300-399 | Redirection | 301 Moved Permanently, 302 Found |\n| 400-499 | Client Errors | 400 Bad Request, 401 Unauthorized, 404 Not Found |\n| 500-599 | Server Errors | 500 Internal Error, 503 Service Unavailable |\n\n### Correct Status Codes\n\n```ts\n// ✅ GOOD: Specific status codes\n200  // GET: Resource retrieved\n201  // POST: Resource created\n204  // DELETE: Resource deleted (no content)\n400  // Bad Request: Validation failed\n401  // Unauthorized: Not authenticated\n403  // Forbidden: Authenticated but no permission\n404  // Not Found: Resource doesn''t exist\n409  // Conflict: Duplicate email\n422  // Unprocessable Entity: Semantic error\n429  // Too Many Requests: Rate limited\n500  // Internal Server Error: Server bug\n\n// ❌ BAD: Vague status codes\n200  // Success response for everything\n500  // Error response for everything\n200  // Returned even when validation failed\n```\n\n## Error Response Format (RFC 7807)\n\n### Problem Details Structure\n\n```ts\n// RFC 7807 Problem Details\ntype ProblemDetails = {\n  type: string;        // URL to error type documentation\n  title: string;       // Short error title\n  status: number;      // HTTP status code\n  detail: string;      // Specific error details\n  instance?: string;   // Request ID for tracking\n  errors?: Record<string, string[]>;  // Field-level errors\n};\n```\n\n### Implementation\n\n```ts\n// lib/errors.ts\nexport class ApiError extends Error {\n  constructor(\n    public status: number,\n    public title: string,\n    public detail: string,\n    public type: string = ''about:blank'',\n    public errors?: Record<string, string[]>\n  ) {\n    super(detail);\n    this.name = ''ApiError'';\n  }\n\n  toJSON() {\n    return {\n      type: this.type,\n      title: this.title,\n      status: this.status,\n      detail: this.detail,\n      instance: this.instance,\n      ...(this.errors && { errors: this.errors })\n    };\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Error Responses\n\n```ts\n// ✅ GOOD: RFC 7807 format\n{\n  \"type\": \"https://api.example.com/errors/validation-failed\",\n  \"title\": \"Validation Failed\",\n  \"status\": 400,\n  \"detail\": \"The request body contains invalid data\",\n  \"instance\": \"req-12345\",\n  \"errors\": {\n    \"email\": [\"Invalid email format\"],\n    \"age\": [\"Must be >= 18\"]\n  }\n}\n\n// ✅ GOOD: Unauthorized (no sensitive details)\n{\n  \"type\": \"https://api.example.com/errors/unauthorized\",\n  \"title\": \"Unauthorized\",\n  \"status\": 401,\n  \"detail\": \"Authentication required\",\n  \"instance\": \"req-12346\"\n}\n\n// ❌ BAD: Leaks internal details\n{\n  \"error\": \"User not found in database\",\n  \"stack\": \"Error: query failed at line 42...\"\n}\n\n// ❌ BAD: Not structured\n{\n  \"message\": \"Something went wrong\"\n}\n```\n\n## Centralized Error Handler\n\n```ts\n// middleware/error-handler.ts\nimport { NextRequest, NextResponse } from ''next/server'';\nimport { ApiError } from ''@/lib/errors'';\n\nexport function errorHandler(error: unknown) {\n  const requestId = crypto.randomUUID();\n\n  // Log error (internal, never exposed)\n  console.error(`[${requestId}] Error:`, error);\n\n  // ApiError (predictable)\n  if (error instanceof ApiError) {\n    return NextResponse.json(\n      {\n        type: error.type,\n        title: error.title,\n        status: error.status,\n        detail: error.detail,\n        instance: requestId,\n        ...(error.errors && { errors: error.errors })\n      },\n      { status: error.status }\n    );\n  }\n\n  // Validation error\n  if (error instanceof ZodError) {\n    return NextResponse.json(\n      {\n        type: ''https://api.example.com/errors/validation-failed'',\n        title: ''Validation Failed'',\n        status: 400,\n        detail: ''The request body contains invalid data'',\n        instance: requestId,\n        errors: error.flatten().fieldErrors\n      },\n      { status: 400 }\n    );\n  }\n\n  // Unknown error (generic message)\n  return NextResponse.json(\n    {\n      type: ''https://api.example.com/errors/internal-server-error'',\n      title: ''Internal Server Error'',\n      status: 500,\n      detail: ''An unexpected error occurred'',\n      instance: requestId\n    },\n    { status: 500 }\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Using Error Handler\n\n```ts\n// app/api/users/route.ts\nimport { errorHandler } from ''@/middleware/error-handler'';\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  try {\n    const body = await request.json();\n\n    // Validate\n    const validated = CreateUserSchema.parse(body);\n\n    // Check duplicate\n    const existing = await db.user.findUnique({\n      where: { email: validated.email }\n    });\n\n    if (existing) {\n      throw new ApiError(\n        409,\n        ''Conflict'',\n        ''A user with this email already exists'',\n        ''https://api.example.com/errors/duplicate-email''\n      );\n    }\n\n    // Create\n    const user = await db.user.create({ data: validated });\n\n    return new Response(JSON.stringify(user), {\n      status: 201,\n      headers: { ''Content-Type'': ''application/json'' }\n    });\n  } catch (error) {\n    return errorHandler(error);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Input Validation\n\n### Schema Validation\n\n```ts\nimport { z } from ''zod'';\n\nconst CreateUserSchema = z.object({\n  email: z.string().email(''Invalid email format''),\n  name: z.string().min(1, ''Name required'').max(255),\n  age: z.number().int().min(0).max(150),\n  role: z.enum([''admin'', ''user'', ''guest'']).default(''user'')\n});\n\n// Validate request\nconst validated = CreateUserSchema.parse(body);\n```\n\n### Sanitization\n\n```ts\nimport DOMPurify from ''isomorphic-dompurify'';\n\nconst sanitized = {\n  ...validated,\n  name: DOMPurify.sanitize(validated.name)\n};\n```\n\n## Rate Limiting\n\n```ts\nimport rateLimit from ''express-rate-limit'';\n\n// General rate limiter\nconst limiter = rateLimit({\n  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,  // 15 minutes\n  max: 100,                   // 100 requests per window\n  message: ''Too many requests, please try again later'',\n  standardHeaders: true,      // Return rate limit info in headers\n  legacyHeaders: false\n});\n\n// Auth rate limiter (stricter)\nconst authLimiter = rateLimit({\n  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,\n  max: 5,                      // 5 attempts\n  skipSuccessfulRequests: true // Don''t count successful logins\n});\n\napp.post(''/login'', authLimiter, loginHandler);\napp.use(''/api/'', limiter);\n```\n\n## Response Formatting\n\n### Success Response\n\n```ts\n// ✅ GOOD: Consistent response\nexport async function GET(request: Request) {\n  const users = await db.user.findMany();\n\n  return NextResponse.json({\n    status: ''success'',\n    data: users,\n    meta: {\n      count: users.length,\n      timestamp: new Date().toISOString()\n    }\n  });\n}\n\n// ✅ GOOD: Paginated response\nexport async function GET(request: Request) {\n  const page = parseInt(request.nextUrl.searchParams.get(''page'') || ''1'');\n  const limit = parseInt(request.nextUrl.searchParams.get(''limit'') || ''20'');\n  const offset = (page - 1) * limit;\n\n  const [users, total] = await Promise.all([\n    db.user.findMany({ skip: offset, take: limit }),\n    db.user.count()\n  ]);\n\n  return NextResponse.json({\n    status: ''success'',\n    data: users,\n    meta: {\n      pagination: {\n        page,\n        limit,\n        total,\n        pages: Math.ceil(total / limit)\n      }\n    }\n  });\n}\n```\n\n## Request Correlation\n\n```ts\n// middleware/correlation-id.ts\nimport { NextResponse } from ''next/server'';\nimport type { NextRequest } from ''next/server'';\n\nexport function middleware(request: NextRequest) {\n  const correlationId = \n    request.headers.get(''x-correlation-id'') || \n    crypto.randomUUID();\n\n  const response = NextResponse.next();\n  response.headers.set(''x-correlation-id'', correlationId);\n\n  return response;\n}\n\n// Include in logs\nconsole.log(`[${correlationId}] User created:`, user);\n\n// Client can track requests\nfetch(''/api/users'', {\n  headers: { ''x-correlation-id'': myRequestId }\n});\n```\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n```ts\n// ❌ BAD: Leaking stack traces\n{\n  \"error\": \"Cannot read property ''id'' of undefined at getUserData (line 42)\",\n  \"stack\": \"Error: ...\\nat app.js:42...\"\n}\n\n// ❌ BAD: Generic error message\n{\n  \"error\": \"Something went wrong\"\n}\n\n// ❌ BAD: No rate limiting\n// Anyone can hammer API endpoint\n\n// ❌ BAD: Overusing 500\n// Always return 500 for any error\n\n// ❌ BAD: No validation\nconst user = await db.user.create(request.body);\n// Raw user input!\n```\n\n## Verification Before Production\n\n- [ ] HTTP status codes specific and appropriate\n- [ ] Error responses RFC 7807 compliant\n- [ ] No stack traces or sensitive data exposed\n- [ ] Input validated on server side\n- [ ] Input sanitized before storage\n- [ ] Rate limiting configured\n- [ ] Correlation IDs for request tracking\n- [ ] Error messages user-friendly (not technical)\n- [ ] Centralized error handler\n- [ ] Response format consistent\n\n## Integration with Project Standards\n\nEnforces security and usability:\n- S-1: No sensitive data in errors\n- C-10: Input validated\n- AP-8: Validation on server side\n\n## Resources\n\n- RFC 7807 Problem Details: https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7807\n- HTTP Status Codes: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Status\n- Express Rate Limiting: https://github.com/nfriedly/express-rate-limit\n---\n\n**Last Updated:** January 24, 2026\n**Compatibility:** Claude Opus 4.5, Claude Code v2.x\n**Status:** Production Ready\n\n> **January 2026 Update:** This skill is compatible with Claude Opus 4.5 and Claude Code v2.x. For complex tasks, use the `effort: high` parameter for thorough analysis.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T09:49:38.572Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Cloud Agents requiring robust REST API development with proper error handling and validation.","zh":"适用于需要强大的REST API开发以及适当错误处理和验证的云代理。","ja":"強力なREST API開発と適切なエラーハンドリングおよびバリデーションを必要とするクラウドエージェントに適しています。","ko":"강력한 REST API 개발 및 적절한 오류 처리 및 유효성 검증이 필요한 클라우드 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Cloud que requieren un desarrollo de API REST robusto con un manejo de errores y validación adecuados.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents Cloud nécessitant un développement d''API REST robuste avec une gestion d''erreurs et une validation appropriées.","de":"Ideal für Cloud-Agents, die eine robuste REST-API-Entwicklung mit ordnungsgemäßer Fehlerbehandlung und Validierung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Nuvem que exigem desenvolvimento robusto de REST API com tratamento e validação adequados de erros.","ru":"Идеально подходит для облачных агентов, требующих надежного развития REST API с правильной обработкой и проверкой ошибок.","ar":"مثالي لعميل السحابة الذي يتطلب تطوير REST API قوي مع معالجة خطأ صحيحة و التحقق"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build secure and scalable APIs using HTTP status codes, RFC 7807 Problem Details for errors, and consistent response formatting, while also implementing rate limiting and security-first error messages.","zh":"赋予代理构建安全且可扩展的API的能力，使用HTTP状态代码、RFC 7807问题详细信息进行错误处理和一致的响应格式，同时实施速率限制和以安全为优先的错误消息。","ja":"HTTPステータスコード、RFC 7807の問題の詳細を使用したエラーハンドリング、一貫したレスポンス形式、およびレート制限を実施しながら、安全でスケーラブルなAPIを構築するエージェントの能力を付与します。","ko":"HTTP 상태 코드, RFC 7807 문제 세부 정보를 사용한 오류 처리 및 일관된 응답 형식과 동시에 속도 제한 및 보안 우선 오류 메시지를 구현하면서 안전하고 확장 가능한 API를 구축할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 부여합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear API seguras y escalables utilizando códigos de estado HTTP, detalles de problemas RFC 7807 para errores y formatos de respuesta consistentes, al mismo tiempo que implementan una limitación de velocidad y mensajes de error con prioridad a la seguridad.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des API sécurisées et évolutives en utilisant des codes d''état HTTP, des détails de problèmes RFC 7807 pour les erreurs et des formats de réponse cohérents, tout en mettant en œuvre une limitation de débit et des messages d''erreur sécurisés.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, sichere und skalierbare APIs mit HTTP-Statuscodes, RFC 7807-Problem-details für Fehler und konsistente Antwortformate zu erstellen, während sie auch eine Rate Limiting und sicherheitsorientierte Fehlermeldungen implementieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir APIs seguras e escaláveis usando códigos de status HTTP, detalhes de problemas RFC 7807 para erros e formatação de resposta consistente, além de implementar limitação de taxa e mensagens de erro com segurança.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать безопасные и масштабируемые API, используя коды состояния HTTP, детали проблем RFC 7807 для ошибок и последовательную форматировку ответа, а также реализацию ограничения скорости и сообщений об ошибках с учетом безопасности.","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من بناء واجهات برمجة تطبيقات آمنة ومقیاسها باستخدام رموز حالة HTTP و تفاصيل مشاكل RFC 7807 للأخطاء وتنسيق استجابة متسق، بالإضافة إلى تنفيذ حد السعر والأخطاء الأمنية أولاً"},"useCases":{"en":["Designing API routes with input validation and sanitization","Implementing centralized error handling with request correlation IDs","Developing APIs with consistent response formats and rate limiting"],"zh":["使用输入验证和清理设计API路由","使用请求相关ID实现集中式错误处理","使用一致的响应格式和速率限制开发API"],"ja":["入力バリデーションとサニタイズを使用してAPIルートを設計する","リクエスト相関IDを使用して集中エラーハンドリングを実装する","一貫したレスポンス形式とレート制限を使用してAPIを開発する"],"ko":["입력 유효성 검사 및 정화로 API 경로를 설계","요청 상관관계 ID를 사용하여 집중식 오류 처리를 구현","일관된 응답 형식 및 속도 제한을 사용하여 API 개발"],"es":["Diseñar rutas de API con validación y saneamiento de entrada","Implementar un manejo de errores centralizado con IDs de correlación de solicitudes","Desarrollar API con formatos de respuesta consistentes y limitación de velocidad"],"fr":["Concevoir des routes d''API avec validation et assainissement des entrées","Mettre en œuvre une gestion d''erreurs centralisée avec des ID de corrélation de requêtes","Développer des API avec des formats de réponses cohérents et une limitation de débit"],"de":["API-Routen mit Eingabevalidierung und -säuberung entwerfen","Zentrales Fehlerhandling mit Anfragekorrelations-IDs implementieren","APIs mit konsistenten Antwortformaten und Rate Limiting entwickeln"],"pt":["Projetar rotas de API com validação e sanitização de entrada","Implementar tratamento centralizado de erros com IDs de correlação de solicitação","Desenvolver APIs com formatos de resposta consistentes e limitação de taxa"],"ru":["Проектирование маршрутов API с проверкой и санитизацией входных данных","Реализация централизованного обработки ошибок с идентификаторами корреляции запросов","Разработка API с последовательными форматами ответа и ограничением скорости"],"ar":["تصميم مسارات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات مع التحقق والتنظيف المدخلات","تنفيذ معالجة مركزية للأخطاء مع معرّفات ارتباط الطلبات","تطوير واجهات برمجة التطبيقات مع تنسيقات استجابة متسقة وحد السعر"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of HTTP status codes and RFC 7807","Limited to REST API development","Needs consideration for security and rate limiting"],"zh":["需要HTTP状态代码和RFC 7807的知识","仅限REST API开发","需要考虑安全性和速率限制"],"ja":["HTTPステータスコードとRFC 7807の知識が必要","REST API開発のみ","セキュリティとレート制限についての考慮が必要"],"ko":["HTTP 상태 코드 및 RFC 7807에 대한 지식 필요","REST API 개발만 해당","보안 및 속도 제한에 대한 고려 필요"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de códigos de estado HTTP y RFC 7807","Limitado al desarrollo de API REST","Necesita consideración para la seguridad y la limitación de velocidad"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance des codes d''état HTTP et de la RFC 7807","Limité au développement d''API REST","Nécessite une prise en compte de la sécurité et de la limitation de débit"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse von HTTP-Statuscodes und RFC 7807","Begrenzt auf die Entwicklung von REST-APIs","Benötigt Berücksichtigung von Sicherheit und Rate Limiting"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento de códigos de status HTTP e RFC 7807","Limitado ao desenvolvimento de REST API","Necessita consideração para segurança e limitação de taxa"],"ru":["Требует знания кодов состояния HTTP и RFC 7807","Ограничен разработкой REST API","Требует учета безопасности и ограничения скорости"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة رموز حالة HTTP و RFC 7807","محدود لتطوير واجهة برمجة التطبيقات REST","يحتاج إلى اعتبار الأمن وحد السعر"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"e1489fbfe053bd90b44f2f7bebdc22b3c262c6d553777679a5321ad9f0705e80","qualityScore":85}');
